.TH sane\-xerox_mfp 5 "15 Dec 2008" "@PACKAGEVERSION@" "SANE Scanner Access Now Easy"
.IX sane\-xerox_mfp
.SH NAME
sane\-xerox_mfp \- SANE backend for Xerox Phaser 3200MFP device et al.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B sane\-xerox_mfp
library implements a SANE (Scanner Access Now Easy) backend that provides
access to several Samsung-based Samsung, Xerox, and Dell scanners.
Please see full list of supported devices at
.IR http://www.sane\-project.org/sane\-supported\-devices.html .

.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.I @CONFIGDIR@/xerox_mfp.conf
USB scanners do not need any configuration.

For a supported scanner in network mode you can specify
.PP
.RS
.B tcp host_address [port]
.RE
.PP
The
.B host_address
is passed through resolver, thus can be a dotted quad or a name from
.I /etc/hosts
or resolvable through DNS.
The default TCP port is 9400.
.PP
To enable automatic discovery of Samsung network scanners, specify
.PP
.RS
.B tcp auto [interface]
.RE
.PP
Discovery sends SNMPv1 GetNext requests using the
.B public
community to UDP port 161 on active local IPv4 broadcast interfaces.
The optional
.B interface
restricts discovery to a named interface, for example
.BR "tcp auto eth0" .
Devices must expose Samsung's DeviceID scalar and report the SCN scanner
capability. Each candidate is verified using the normal scanner inquiry
on TCP port 9400.
.PP
The discovery reply window is one second, shared across interfaces, with
three requests per interface. Candidate verification has a shared five-second
budget; an inquiry already in progress can finish after that budget.
At most 16 interface addresses and 32 distinct scanner addresses are processed.
Discovery is disabled by default. It requires a build with Net-SNMP support
(configure option --with-snmp), interface enumeration and a monotonic clock
on the host platform. Builds without Net-SNMP support still accept manual
network configuration. IPv6, routed discovery, other SNMP
communities and devices without the Samsung DeviceID scalar require manual
configuration. Firewalls must allow the UDP replies to the client's
ephemeral port.
.PP
Manual entries and discovery can be combined. Aliases of the same IPv4
address and TCP port appear only once, using the first configured name.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @CONFIGDIR@/xerox_mfp.conf
The backend configuration file. By default all scanner types/models are enabled, you
may want to comment out unwanted entries.
.TP
.I @LIBDIR@/libsane\-xerox_mfp.a
The static library implementing this backend.
.TP
.I @LIBDIR@/libsane\-xerox_mfp.so
The shared library implementing this backend (present on systems that
support dynamic loading).

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SANE_DEBUG_XEROX_MFP
If the library was compiled with debug support enabled, this
environment variable controls the debug level for this backend.  Higher
debug levels increase the verbosity of the output.

Example:
export SANE_DEBUG_XEROX_MFP=4

.SH LIMITATIONS
Automatic discovery is limited to local IPv4 networks and the Samsung
DeviceID scalar; it has been tested with the M2070 Series. IPv6 addressing
has never been tested.

